# CacheUtility Project Overview

## Project Purpose
CacheUtility is a thread-safe, generic wrapper for `System.Runtime.Caching` that provides advanced caching features for .NET applications. It is distributed as a NuGet package and supports:

- Thread-safe memory caching with lock-free hot paths (`ConcurrentDictionary` + `Lazy<T>` populate dedup)
- Sync (`Get<T>`) and async (`GetAsync<T>`) populate methods, with single-flight de-duplication
- `TryGet<T>` for cache-only lookups (never invokes populate)
- Cache groups with strongly-typed bulk access (`GetAllByGroup<T>`)
- Cycle-safe dependency relationships between groups (`SetDependencies`)
- Multiple expiration strategies (sliding / absolute) and non-blocking auto-refresh
- Optional persistent cache to disk (atomic writes, group whitelist, background cleanup, `Persist` for in-place changes)
- Built-in diagnostic logging via `Microsoft.Extensions.Logging` (`AddCacheLogging()`)

