## Main Class: Cache
`Cache` is declared `public abstract class` with only static members, so it cannot be instantiated. Public surface:

- `Get<TData>(...)` / `GetAsync<TData>(...)` - retrieve or populate, with sync or async populate methods
- `TryGet<TData>(key, group, out value)` - cache-only lookup, never populates
- `Remove(key, group)`, `Remove(List<string>, group)`, `RemoveGroup(params string[])`, `RemoveAllButThese(...)`, `RemoveAll()`
- `GetAllByGroup(group)` and `GetAllByGroup<TData>(group)` - bulk retrieval
- `SetDependencies(group, params dependents)` - cascade-on-remove relationships
- `Persist(key, group)` - write an entry's current in-memory value to disk after an in-place change (1.4.7)
- `EnablePersistentCache(...)`, `DisablePersistentCache()`, `IsPersistentCacheEnabled`, `GetPersistentCacheOptions()`, `GetPersistentCacheStatistics()`, `CleanupExpiredPersistentCache()`
- `GetAllCacheMetadata()` - diagnostic snapshot of every cached item
- `ConfigureLogging(ILoggerFactory)` - wire up logging in non-DI scenarios

Internally, every cached value is wrapped in `Cache.CacheItem<T>` (which implements an internal `ICacheItem` interface, used to avoid reflection on hot paths like metadata enumeration and size estimation).
